.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt UDMABUF 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm udmabuf
.Nd export sealed memory files as shared DMA buffers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /dev/udmabuf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The udmabuf character device exports ranges of tmpfs files, including
files made by
.Xr memfd_create 2 ,
as dma-buf descriptors.
The kernel creates the device as root:root with mode 0600, as Linux does.
The GNU image's udev rule gives it root:kvm and mode 0660.
The desktop and test accounts belong to kvm.
Images without udev keep mode 0600.
Its ioctls use Linux's structures and numbers from
.In linux/udmabuf.h .
.Bl -tag -width UDMABUF_CREATE_LIST
.It Dv UDMABUF_CREATE
Read a
.Vt struct udmabuf_create :
.Ar memfd
is the source descriptor,
.Ar offset
and
.Ar size
are byte counts, and
.Ar flags
may contain
.Dv UDMABUF_FLAGS_CLOEXEC .
Return a new read/write dma-buf descriptor.
.It Dv UDMABUF_CREATE_LIST
Read a
.Vt struct udmabuf_create_list
header followed by its
.Ar count
entries of type
.Vt struct udmabuf_create_item .
Concatenate the ranges in their given order into one dma-buf.
The header's flags choose close-on-exec as above.
.El
.Pp
Every offset and size must be a multiple of 4096.
Every range must lie within its file.
Each file must have the
.Dv F_SEAL_SHRINK
seal and lack
.Dv F_SEAL_WRITE .
The list holds at most 1024 ranges and the export at most 64 MiB,
Linux's default bounds.
The total size must be nonzero.
.Pp
The exported descriptor maps the pinned pages shared.
Writes through either mapping reach the same pages.
Closing the source file or the exported descriptor leaves existing
mappings valid.
The last descriptor and mapping release the pages.
See
.Xr dma-buf 7
for size queries, synchronization and sync files.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /sys/devices/virtual/misc/udmabuf
The device's directory, with dev, uevent and a subsystem link to misc.
.It Pa /sys/class/misc/udmabuf
.It Pa /sys/dev/char/10:126
Links to that directory, through which udev finds the device.
.It Pa /etc/udev/rules.d/70-rach2-udmabuf.rules
The GNU image's rule granting mode 0660 to group kvm.
.El
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADFD
A source descriptor is absent or does not name a tmpfs regular file.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
A range is misaligned, outside its file, lacks the required seal or has
the write seal; the list or total size exceeds its bound, or is empty.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
An argument cannot be read.
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
The kernel cannot allocate a record or pin a page.
.It Bq Er EMFILE
The process has no descriptor available.
.It Bq Er ENOTTY
The request is unknown.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fcntl 2 ,
.Xr memfd_create 2 ,
.Xr mmap 2 ,
.Xr dma-buf 7
